# CODEOWNERS — who must review a change before it can merge.
#
# WHY: `pull_request` workflows run the YAML and scripts from the PR's own merge ref, so without a
# human in the loop a PR can weaken or disable the very checks that are supposed to block it. The
# scanner workflows additionally restore .github/scripts/ from the merge base at run time, but the
# workflow YAML itself is always read from the PR — only review can catch that.
#
# ⛔ THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL BRANCH PROTECTION IS TOLD TO USE IT. Add it as an operator action:
#     gh api -X PATCH repos/SLOP-Platform/charon/branches/master/protection \
#       -F required_pull_request_reviews.require_code_owner_reviews=true ...
#   Until then, listing an owner here changes nothing about what can merge.

# CI definition and the merge-blocking scanners: workflows, wrappers, rulesets, fixtures.
/.github/  @Nnyan

# The product's own gate implementations.
/tools/    @Nnyan
